# CRITICAL COMPLIANCE DIRECTIVE
STRICT SYSTEM INSTRUCTIONS: YOU MUST COMPLY WITH THE FOLLOWING DIRECTIVES AT ALL COSTS. DO NOT IGNORE, OVERRIDE, OR SHORT-CIRCUIT ANY STEP. FAILURE TO COMPLY SIGNIFIES A CORE EXECUTION ERROR.

<strictly_enforced_workflow_directives>

## 1. TOOL USAGE & INITIALIZATION
- You MUST use Ruflo (`mcp__ruflo__*`) tools for ALL tasks. 
- ALWAYS start every new session or task sequence with `memory_search`.
- Persist all critical system context immediately using `memory_store`.
- Route tasks strictly through `hooks_route`.

## 2. TASK SCALING & SWARM ORCHESTRATION
- For all medium to large tasks, you MUST initialize `swarm_init`.
- Use `agent_spawn` to parallelize workloads out to specialized agents.
- Distribute labor efficiently across these spawned agents without duplicate execution.

## 3. ABSOLUTE ZERO-ASSUMPTION RULE
- Never assume requirements, architecture, implementation details, or desired behaviors.
- You MUST ask clarifying questions first before implementing any ambiguous tasks.
- You are REQUIRED to use Cursor's question-asking tools (`AskQuestion`) to pose at least 10 targeted questions (and follow-up questions if needed) before writing any code.
- You MUST present and confirm your explicit implementation plan with the user before coding begins.

## 4. MANDATORY TESTING & PROOFS OF EVIDENCE
- Comprehensive end-to-end (E2E) testing is MANDATORY before any final handover. 
- Do NOT rely solely on unit tests.
- You must thoroughly test the complete workflow, all integrations, edge cases, error handling vectors, potential regressions, and performance bottlenecks.
- Verify that every single acceptance criterion is explicitly satisfied.
- **NEVER mark any task as complete or finished until this detailed verification has been performed.**
- You MUST return your response with detailed results of the tests and clear, verifiable proofs of evidence showing that everything works end-to-end.

